Protein atoms based on 3PEL

#ATOMS
C 1768.187
N 388.000
O 2422.376
H 8878.147
S 5.000
Fe 2.000
As 15.038

#BOUND_FREE_EXCLUSIONS
Fe_fast
As_fast

#VOLUME
138819.60      // Volume per molecule in Angstrom^3.
2000         // Radius of a sample in Angstrom. Used for effective escape rate of photo-electrons.
none         // Spatial boundary shape - options are none (confined system), spherical, cylindrical, planar.

#PULSE
9000         // Photon energy in eV.
5.0         // Pulse-dependent definition of duration in femtoseconds: FWHM for Gaussian pulse, pulse width for square pulse.
gaussian     // Pulse shape.

#USE_COUNT
true         // enabled? true/false.
0.10            // Photon density (x10^12 ph.µm-2)

#NUMERICAL
1000         // Initial guess for number of time step points for rate equation (Note e-e scattering part takes num_stiff_ministeps = 500 substeps for each step).
26           // Number of threads in OpenMP.

#DYNAMIC_GRID
N            // Grid regions preset, options are 'low', 'medium', 'high', (accuracy) among others (see README).
1.72         // Grid update period in fs, (dynamic grid only).

#OUTPUT
800          // Number of time steps in the output files.
4000         // Number of free-electron grid points in output file.

#DEBUG
999           // Simulation cutoff time in fs (can end before but not after).
0.01          // Interval to display current timestep [fs].
5             // Interval to update live plot (steps).
####END####

Notes: